## :wheat: How bread rises {.title}

Year 7 science

---

## :microscope: Yeast is alive

- A fungus, one cell each
- It eats sugar and breathes out carbon dioxide
- Warm and wet, it works fast; cold, it sleeps

---

## :wind: Gas needs a net {.two}

- Flour has two proteins
- Water and kneading join them into gluten

|

- Gluten is stretchy
- It traps the gas as tiny bubbles

---

## :flame: Then the oven

- Heat makes the gas expand: oven spring
- At 60 °C the yeast dies
- The crust browns: sugars and proteins, the Maillard reaction

> Ask who has watched dough rise at home.
